I just double-checked my D&D rulebooks, and in them Puddings are split
when attacked by slashing or piercing weapons.  Of course, this could be
one of the many ways that NetHack is intentionally different from D&D, but
I prefer the D&D way of doing it.  So here's a small patch that causes
Puddings to only split when melee attacked by slashing or piercing weapons.


